[["NSE vs BSE (simulated): the same share on India's two exchanges, minute by minute. If you already hold a share, sell it where it's dearer and buy the same number back where it's cheaper; your holding is unchanged and you keep the gap, minus costs. No orders are placed."], ["Costs for a Rs 1,00,000 trade: holdings route (sell from demat, buy back, STT both sides) 0.239%; intraday route (only if your broker lets the legs offset) 0.083%. A gap smaller than that loses money. Trade size: Rs 1,00,000 or what traded on each exchange that minute, whichever is smaller. Profits are an upper bound: the last trade of a minute may no longer be available."], [], ["Two measures: 'same minute' trades at the prices of the minute the gap shows (impossible by hand: the gap is usually two last trades up to a minute apart, and firms next to the exchange take it in milliseconds); 'next minute' places both orders in the following minute and gets that minute's prices, which is what someone watching a screen could do."], ["BY DAY", "Date", "Shares compared", "Minutes compared", "Median gap (%)", "Minutes above holdings cost", "Holdings: gaps", "Holdings: same minute (Rs)", "Holdings: next minute (Rs)", "Holdings: next-minute wins", "Intraday: gaps", "Intraday: same minute (Rs)", "Intraday: next minute (Rs)", "Intraday: next-minute wins"], ["", "'2026-11-05", 493, 135824, 0.0415, 1193, 1142, 95273.7, -106122.92, 25, 19830, 553417.89, -596920.14, 1721], ["", "'2026-11-04", 493, 122281, 0.044, 966, 920, 52070.4, -76044.69, 16, 18835, 440460.13, -459358.02, 1532], ["", "'2026-11-03", 493, 120602, 0.0435, 1066, 1024, 78033.05, -74832.53, 27, 17800, 450757.73, -420041.52, 1405], ["", "'2026-11-02", 493, 124241, 0.0443, 1104, 1069, 77156.99, -75615.44, 17, 19590, 472256.99, -485735.88, 1616], ["", "'2026-10-30", 493, 122172, 0.045, 1283, 1221, 88388.51, -75632.92, 24, 20125, 493738.21, -475017.78, 1674], ["", "'2026-10-29", 493, 118003, 0.0462, 1035, 1004, 64845.76, -67739.27, 17, 18877, 429588